  "adaptation_contract": [
    "macOS Chrome discovery and native display",
    "package-local XIUXIAN imports",
    "memory-only production broker with the reference one-shot contract",
    "deduplicate dynamic windows and require all declared windows before done",
    "server perfect only when explicitly confirmed",
    "await cancelled hit tasks before releasing the account transport",
    "response-aware hold rescue bounded by perfect arrival and actual local hold",
    "exclude deliberate hold rescue from network drift feedback",
    "scheduler lateness excludes arrival compensation",
    "use partial hold-rescue slack with asymmetric-transit margin and ticket-age ceiling",
    "space dynamic-window reads from request start at the official 360 ms cadence, with only one read in flight",
    "reschedule pending charge and release timers on arrived timing feedback without replaying submitted actions",
    "publish account-bound per-window plans and observed lifecycle separately from official hit confirmation",
    "retain the original serial worker semantics inside each account shard while running six account-isolated shards in parallel with separate native profiles",
    "scope verifier capability and lifecycle to the owning account so one shard failure cannot gate the fleet",
    "hold each account process lease for the full verifier profile lifecycle and close every shard exception-safely",
    "reject symlinked profile path components and revalidate profile containment before every shard and browser start",
    "prepare only the public official page during a validated admission period without generating credentials",
    "use recent same-account start RTT only for clearly inflated begin clock estimates",
    "bound each dynamic-window read and return retry ownership to the reveal loop",
    "retain official damage multipliers and classify reduced damage separately from perfect hit counts",
    "register absolute event-loop deadlines before yielding so scheduler stalls are not slept twice",
    "continue the same dynamic-window cursor after local stalls until an authoritative server completion condition",
    "bound dynamic-window reads to one second and pace all retryable reads from request start",
    "wait real challenge minDurationMs before finish and preserve the official short-duration error code",
    "ignore slow or retried request timing when learning persistent hold skew",
    "reconcile local hit receipts with valid server finish hits and perfects without rewriting receipts",
    "exclude upstream disk checkpoint recovery so initData, session tokens, and one-shot verification material remain memory-only"
  ],
